  "notes": "The portal has carved mouldings and a shallow gable between shoulder stones. Buttress caps finish in narrow points. Window tracery is rectangular. Bay counts on obscured faces and dimensions of openings are estimates. The narrow westward range occupies the position of the adjoining Molecular Biology Laboratory on the Western facilities map. The high roof covers the northern spine, with a lower return above the entire south frontage."
